  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_036 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 acc. In RNA-only experiments, avgpool consistently outperformed transformer aggregation (pca: 0.591 vs 0.519; scvi: 0.650 vs untested), but that evidence comes from weaker encoder combinations. The key remaining uncertainty for the top-performing multimodal setup is whether transformer aggregation could exploit cross-profile interactions more effectively when paired with the strong ViT image features. config_038 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer (keeping concat fusion, which slightly beat weighted), directly testing this interaction. If transformer improves performance, it opens a new optimization axis; if it confirms avgpool superiority, we can confidently lock in the aggregation choice and focus remaining budget on other design dimensions. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the last untested design variable in the strongest configuration family."
}

